const e="indian-school-talent-fest-oman",c=2025,t="Built from the ISTF 2025 Handbook (Indian School Al Maabela, 38 pages) and the Indian School Nizwa circular on ISTF 2026. The handbook prints no entry fee and no ages (classes only). The 2026 handbook was not available. The Nizwa circular's school-level Google Form links, classroom code and school coordinator phone numbers belong to one member school and are not copied. The personal e-mail address printed for the Wonder Weavers' Talent video submissions is not copied. The 2024 edition circular (Indian School Bousher, 39 events hosted by Indian School Wadi Kabir, 26 and 27 October 2024) and the ISTF 2021 handbook (virtual edition, Indian School Darsait) were read; only the 2021 entry-limit table is kept, as past-edition information.",o=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Indian School Talent Fest (ISTF), Indian Schools in Oman. Read these rules before you register.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"ISTF is held on {{EventDates}} at {{Venue}}. Send the entry form with the participant photographs by {{RegistrationDeadline}} to {{RegistrationEmail}}. Teacher Coordinators confirm their entry list at the ISTF Office on the first day ({{ReconfirmationTime}}).","Notes":["Participants should carry a photo ID from their school.","Never reveal the identity of your school to the judges or the audience, by words, deeds or uniform.","Contact: {{LeadCoordinator}}."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["The Indian School Talent Fest is held under the aegis of the Board of Directors, Indian Schools in Oman. One member school hosts it each year.","There are 33 competitive events: 19 solo events in three stages by class and 14 group events in the Open category. Each event page has its own rules.","UTAR (Unique Talent Recognition) and Wonder Weavers' Talent (for children with special needs) are non-competitive events. They are not scored.","An event is cancelled if it has fewer than three entries. Schools are told by {{CancellationNoticeDate}}.","Interference by students or parents of any school in the smooth running of the programme is not allowed inside the school campus. No one may talk to the judges of the events.","Entry for the audience is restricted. The host school sends invitations to the schools for staff and participants.","Take care of your valuables. The organisers take no responsibility for them.","All participating students and teachers in charge get food and refreshments. Teachers collect the food coupon at the ISTF Office when registering on both festival days at 7:00 a.m.","Free accommodation for out-stationed schools is provided on the school campus on request. Students bring bedding or a sleeping bag; accompanying teachers get bedding on request. A school that prefers a hotel can have one arranged and pays the cost. Contact: {{AccommodationContact}}.","The themes, dialogues, costumes, choreography and make-up of every event must suit school competitions and respect the culture and traditions of the Sultanate of Oman. Any violation leads to disqualification."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["ISTF is an open competition for students from class I to class XII. The competitive events are for classes III to XII.","Sub-Junior stage (Blossoms): students of classes III to V, solo events.","Junior stage (Juventa): students of classes VI to VIII, solo events.","Senior stage (Titans): students of classes IX, X, XI and XII, solo events.","Open category (Galaxies): students of classes III to XII, group events.","Entries are sent by schools. Every school can send up to two students to each solo event.","A student may take part in only one event in the morning session and one in the afternoon session. The timings of events must not clash. The schedule of the morning and afternoon sessions is sent by email. This rule does not apply to Digital Photography and Album Making and to Digital Ad Making.","Each participant needs a photo ID from their school.","For each participant, the school gives the full name as per the school registration, the class and the gender. For classical dance events it also gives the dance style."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Send the completed entry form, with the photographs of the participants, to {{RegistrationEmail}} by {{RegistrationDeadline}}.","Send any change of participant names to {{RegistrationEmail}} on or before {{NameChangeDeadline}}.","Photographs: send good quality photographs of every participant and team in school uniform, with the registration form or on a USB, by {{RegistrationDeadline}}. Specification: {{PhotoSpec}}.","Solo participants send a passport-size photograph. File name: {{SoloPhotoFileName}}.","Each group event entry sends a team group photograph. File name: {{TeamPhotoFileName}}.","On the first day, the Teacher Coordinators report to the ISTF Office to reconfirm the entry list: {{ReconfirmationTime}}.","Digital Ad Making: put both video files in the Google Drive that the host school shares with the School Coordinator, by {{AdSubmissionDeadline}}.","Send feedback and suggestions to {{RegistrationEmail}}."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees","Items":["{{EntryFee}}.","The only fee printed is the grievance fee: {{GrievanceFee}}."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates and Times","Items":["The festival is on {{EventDates}}.","Registration closes on {{RegistrationDeadline}}. Names can be changed until {{NameChangeDeadline}}.","Inauguration: {{InauguralTime}}.","Valedictory function: {{ValedictoryTime}}.","Reporting at event venues: {{SessionReportingTimes}}.","UTAR entries: {{UtarUsbDeadline}}. Wonder Weavers' Talent videos: by {{CwsnVideoDeadline}}."]},{"Key":"venue","Title":"Venue","Items":["The venue is {{Venue}}.","Contact the Principal's Office on {{SchoolOffice}}."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Points and Grades","Items":["Every event is judged by five criteria. Each criterion is given 10 points, so each event is out of 50 marks.","The scores are collated and the final scores are graded A+ (Outstanding), A (Excellent), B+ (Very good) and B (Good).","Merit Certificates go to the first quarter above the mean point (A+), the second quarter above the mean (A), the third quarter above the mean (B+) and the fourth quarter above the mean (B).","Scores below the mean point get a Participation Certificate. All other participants receive Participation Certificates.","Accompanists are not awarded any certificate.","Championship points for the school: solo events 5, 4, 3, 2 and 1 points; group events 10, 8, 6, 4 and 2 points for the five placings.","If a participant or team goes over the maximum time limit of an event, marks are deducted from the total: up to 30 seconds over = 0 marks, more than 30 seconds over = 5 marks, more than 1 minute over = 10 marks."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes and Certificates","Items":["The school with the most points at the end of all events wins the Indian School Talent Fest Championship Trophy. The first runner-up also gets a trophy.","If two schools tie for the overall winner, they are declared Joint Winners. Both keep the Championship Trophy for a period of time. A lot decides this after the valedictory function.","The results of all events are displayed. All prizes, trophies and certificates are given at the valedictory ceremony.","At the valedictory function, the teacher coordinator and four student representatives go to the stage to take the prizes and mementos for their school, without delay, when the school name is announced. They also stand properly for the official photographer.","Teachers in charge collect their school flags from the Multi-Purpose Hall after the valedictory function.","The best 3 performances of UTAR and of CWSN are shown at the valedictory ceremony on 14 November 2025."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Entries from a School","Items":["Group events: the number of teams and of team members is printed for each event. For example, Roots Rejoice allows two teams of 6 to 8 students, and most dance, band and drama events allow one team.","UTAR: a school sends at least 1 and at most 5 entries, one talent per participant.","Wonder Weavers' Talent: a school sends at least 1 and at most 5 video recordings.","The student team leader of each school, in formal school uniform, carries the school flag at the inaugural function."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and Disqualification","Items":["Dress code and identity: all participants except those in the performing arts competitions are formally or smartly dressed.","The name of the school and the identity of the participant must not be shown before, during or after the event until the results are announced. Do not wear school uniform or introduce yourself to the judges. A participant who reveals their name or school is disqualified immediately.","Each school has a green room for its performing arts participants. Use only the green room given to your school.","Mobile phones are not allowed in the waiting rooms during the event. Only participants and teachers in charge may enter the waiting rooms.","Accompaniment, accompanists and background music (live or recorded) are allowed only if the rules of that event say 'allowed'.","Audio USB: only the audio track of the performance, in a format that plays on Windows Media Player. Hand it to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Write only the chest number on the USB, never a school name or number. Keep a backup audio file.","Chest number: the organisers give each team or participant a chest number. The judges judge by it, so wear it where the judges can see it clearly. Wearing a wrong chest number, or swapping numbers, leads to disqualification.","The teacher in charge or the participant must be at the venue 30 minutes before the event to draw the lot for the chest number. If not, the Event Coordinator decides when the team or participant reports.","Order of performance is only the order of appearance on stage and may not follow the chest number. For Printing Art, Blackout Poetry, Canvas Painting, Clay Modelling, Mandala Art, Collage Making, Illusion Sculpture, Digital Photography and Album Making and Digital Ad Making there is no performance order: participation follows the registration sequence (chest number).","Be fully ready when you report to the venue. No extra time is given for make-up, props, music or practice.","A team or participant who reports more than 30 minutes after the scheduled start can be disqualified.","Three calls are made for each team or participant to come to the stage. A team or participant who does not perform after the third call is disqualified. The organisers decide such matters finally.","Undesirable behaviour by a participant, teacher in charge or parent leads to disqualification of the participant or team.","A team or participant who breaks any rule of the festival is disqualified."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging","Items":["The judges' decision is final and binding in all respects for the final results.","The organiser's decision is final and binding in all matters related to ISTF.","Each event is judged on the five criteria listed on its own page, each worth 10 points."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Complaints and Appeals","Items":["Only the Teacher Coordinator of the participating school may report a grievance, in writing, to the Lead Coordinator at the ISTF Office (A Block, Room No. 3). Students and parents may not.","A grievance must reach the Lead Coordinator within one hour of the declaration of the result, with a fee: {{GrievanceFee}}.","The parties in dispute may be heard. If the grievance is upheld the fee is refunded, otherwise it is forfeited. The decision of the Jury of Appeal is final and binding."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other items in the handbook","Items":["UTAR (Unique Talent Recognition), classes I to XII, solo, non-competitive: up to 5 entries per school, each up to 4 minutes. A school selects the best talents in a school-level round. Schools record the selected talents on video and give two USBs: USB 1 for judging (videos only, a short description of the talent may come before each video, no name of student or school, otherwise the entry is disqualified) and USB 2 for screening (the same videos with the participant details and school information before each video). Hand the USBs to the ISTF Office on the first day before 10:30 a.m. Dress code: formal attire or as the performance needs, no school uniform. Judging criteria, 10 points each: Originality, Confidence, Skill & Execution, Uniqueness, Overall Impact.","Wonder Weavers' Talent, for children with special needs (CSE/CWSN), non-competitive: a school submits 1 to 5 video recordings by Google Drive link by {{CwsnVideoDeadline}}. The host school chooses the best 3 to show at the valedictory ceremony and may invite selected schools to perform live. All submitted entries get a Merit Certificate. Video format MP4 with good audio and visual clarity; file name: School's Abbreviation_Event Name_Name of the participant. Give the full name, class and gender of each participant.","Foundational stage (classes I and II): school-level competitive events in 2026, according to the 2026 circular.","The 2021 virtual edition (Indian School Darsait) set the maximum entries per school by strength of the school (3000 and above: 5 solo and 4 group; 1000 to 3000: 4 and 3; 500 to 1000: 3 and 2; under 500: 2 and 1). The 2025 handbook limits every school to two entries per solo event."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"ISTF 2025 Handbook (Indian School Al Maabela)","Url":"https://ismoman.com/PDFDOCUMENTS/ISTF%202025%20@ISAM%20HANDBOOK%20%2019.10.25.pdf"}]}`),n=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.6 rule 8 and p.12 rule 9",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Every school can send up to two students to each solo event.","Give each participant's full name as per the school registration, the class and the gender.","Send a passport-size photograph. File name: {{SoloPhotoFileName}}."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Every school can send up to two students to each solo event.
- Give each participant's full name as per the school registration, the class and the gender.
- Send a passport-size photograph. File name: {{SoloPhotoFileName}}.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.8 Number of Participants and p.12 rule 9",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The number of teams and the team size are printed for each group event.","Give each team member's full name as per the school registration, the class and the gender.","Send a team group photograph for each event. File name: {{TeamPhotoFileName}}."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- The number of teams and the team size are printed for each group event.
- Give each team member's full name as per the school registration, the class and the gender.
- Send a team group photograph for each event. File name: {{TeamPhotoFileName}}.`}],i=[{AgeGroup:"Blossoms (III-V)",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.6 rules 4 and 8",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Sub-Junior category, Blossoms: students of classes III, IV and V, solo events.","Ages are not printed. The age band in the template is a placeholder, and the class restriction is the rule."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Sub-Junior category, Blossoms: students of classes III, IV and V, solo events.
- Ages are not printed. The age band in the template is a placeholder, and the class restriction is the rule.`},{AgeGroup:"Juventa (VI-VIII)",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.6 rules 5 and 8",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Junior category, Juventa: students of classes VI, VII and VIII, solo events.","Ages are not printed. The age band in the template is a placeholder, and the class restriction is the rule."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Junior category, Juventa: students of classes VI, VII and VIII, solo events.
- Ages are not printed. The age band in the template is a placeholder, and the class restriction is the rule.`},{AgeGroup:"Titans (IX-XII)",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.6 rules 6 and 8",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Senior category, Titans: students of classes IX, X, XI and XII, solo events.","Ages are not printed. The age band in the template is a placeholder, and the class restriction is the rule."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Senior category, Titans: students of classes IX, X, XI and XII, solo events.
- Ages are not printed. The age band in the template is a placeholder, and the class restriction is the rule.`},{AgeGroup:"Galaxies Open (III-XII)",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.6 rules 7 and 8",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Open category, Galaxies: students of classes III to XII, group events.","The 2026 circular prints the Open Category as classes I to XII.","Ages are not printed. The age band in the template is a placeholder, and the class restriction is the rule."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Open category, Galaxies: students of classes III to XII, group events.
- The 2026 circular prints the Open Category as classes I to XII.
- Ages are not printed. The age band in the template is a placeholder, and the class restriction is the rule.`}],a=JSON.parse(`[{"Title":"Mini Theatre","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Mini Theatre","Sections":{"About":["Dramatic recitation in English. Each participant enacts a dramatic lyric on any theme of their own choice, for example The Talking Pencil, The Lost Cloud, The Mobile Phone Speaks, Magic Paintbrush or The Talking Mirror."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Props and costume may be used to show the character, but they must be simple and manageable by the performer alone.","The face of the participant must stay visible throughout and must not be fully covered by a costume, mask or props.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Pre-recorded music, karaoke or live music is not allowed."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Choice & Relevance of Lyrics","Expression (voice modulation, gestures, emotions)","Pronunciation & Clarity of Speech","Creativity of Presentation","Originality & Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Dramatic recitation in English. Each participant enacts a dramatic lyric on any theme of their own choice, for example The Talking Pencil, The Lost Cloud, The Mobile Phone Speaks, Magic Paintbrush or The Talking Mirror.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Props and costume may be used to show the character, but they must be simple and manageable by the performer alone.\\n- The face of the participant must stay visible throughout and must not be fully covered by a costume, mask or props.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Pre-recorded music, karaoke or live music is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Choice & Relevance of Lyrics\\n- Expression (voice modulation, gestures, emotions)\\n- Pronunciation & Clarity of Speech\\n- Creativity of Presentation\\n- Originality & Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Taal Tarang","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Taal Tarang","Sections":{"About":["Indian vocal folk song, solo. Only traditional Indian folk songs are permitted."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["The folk song may be in any recognised Indian language or dialect, but it must be a genuine folk rendition with school-appropriate lyrics.","Participants are encouraged to wear attire that reflects the culture of the folk tradition they present.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Film songs are strictly prohibited.","Pre-programmed or live accompaniment of music is not allowed."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Choice of Song","Rendition","Voice Quality & Expression","Creativity & Improvisation","Overall Presentation & Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Indian vocal folk song, solo. Only traditional Indian folk songs are permitted.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The folk song may be in any recognised Indian language or dialect, but it must be a genuine folk rendition with school-appropriate lyrics.\\n- Participants are encouraged to wear attire that reflects the culture of the folk tradition they present.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs are strictly prohibited.\\n- Pre-programmed or live accompaniment of music is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Choice of Song\\n- Rendition\\n- Voice Quality & Expression\\n- Creativity & Improvisation\\n- Overall Presentation & Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Printopia","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Printopia","Sections":{"About":["Printing art, solo. Theme: Impressions of Nature, shown through handmade stencil printing, vegetable printing, leaf printing and similar methods."],"TimeAndFormat":["The competition lasts 2 hours."],"Rules":["Each participant gets an A3 sheet. Using the drawing paper given by the organisers is compulsory.","Participants bring their own stationery and printing materials (pencils, erasers, sharpeners, rulers and similar).","Pre-cut vegetables can be brought.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Only non-toxic colours are permitted: watercolours, poster colours or acrylics.","No pre-printed, traced or machine-cut designs."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Relevance to Theme","Creativity & Originality","Use of Printing Technique","Execution & Neatness","Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Printing art, solo. Theme: Impressions of Nature, shown through handmade stencil printing, vegetable printing, leaf printing and similar methods.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The competition lasts 2 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each participant gets an A3 sheet. Using the drawing paper given by the organisers is compulsory.\\n- Participants bring their own stationery and printing materials (pencils, erasers, sharpeners, rulers and similar).\\n- Pre-cut vegetables can be brought.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Only non-toxic colours are permitted: watercolours, poster colours or acrylics.\\n- No pre-printed, traced or machine-cut designs.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Relevance to Theme\\n- Creativity & Originality\\n- Use of Printing Technique\\n- Execution & Neatness\\n- Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Kavya Aanchal","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Kavya Aanchal","Sections":{"About":["Hindi poetry recitation, solo. Each contestant recites a poem of their choice."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each participant gets 4 minutes."],"Rules":["Occasional consultation of the poem may be permitted, but reciting from a script loses points.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Appropriate Choice of Poem","Voice and Articulation","Dramatic Appropriateness","Fluency","Overall Performance"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Hindi poetry recitation, solo. Each contestant recites a poem of their choice.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each participant gets 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Occasional consultation of the poem may be permitted, but reciting from a script loses points.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Appropriate Choice of Poem\\n- Voice and Articulation\\n- Dramatic Appropriateness\\n- Fluency\\n- Overall Performance\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Blackout Poetry","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Blackout Poetry","Sections":{"About":["Versification in English, solo. Each participant gets a printed page of text (newspaper, magazine or story) and makes a blackout poem by choosing words and phrases from it. All other words are blacked out with markers, colours or creative designs. The theme is open."],"TimeAndFormat":["The competition lasts 1 hour."],"Rules":["Markers, pens, highlighters and other safe art materials are allowed.","Students are encouraged to use meaningful words, artistic design, patterns or illustrations to improve the look of the poem. Creativity and originality are encouraged.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Creativity & Originality","Word Selection & Poetry","Visual Presentation","Clarity & Coherence","Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Versification in English, solo. Each participant gets a printed page of text (newspaper, magazine or story) and makes a blackout poem by choosing words and phrases from it. All other words are blacked out with markers, colours or creative designs. The theme is open.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The competition lasts 1 hour.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Markers, pens, highlighters and other safe art materials are allowed.\\n- Students are encouraged to use meaningful words, artistic design, patterns or illustrations to improve the look of the poem. Creativity and originality are encouraged.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Creativity & Originality\\n- Word Selection & Poetry\\n- Visual Presentation\\n- Clarity & Coherence\\n- Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Oratory Odyssey","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Oratory Odyssey","Sections":{"About":["Elocution in English, solo. Each participant comes prepared to speak on one topic of their choice from the printed list: Climate Change: Small Actions, Big Impact; Social Media Influence: Connecting or Isolating People?; Fast Fashion and Sustainability: The Hidden Cost of Trendy Clothes; Food Waste: A Global Challenge with Simple Solutions."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each participant gets 4 minutes."],"Rules":["The content must be relevant to the given topics.","Occasional consultation of notes is permitted, but reading from a prepared script loses points.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Content & Relevance","Enunciation","Expression & Engagement","Confidence","Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Elocution in English, solo. Each participant comes prepared to speak on one topic of their choice from the printed list: Climate Change: Small Actions, Big Impact; Social Media Influence: Connecting or Isolating People?; Fast Fashion and Sustainability: The Hidden Cost of Trendy Clothes; Food Waste: A Global Challenge with Simple Solutions.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each participant gets 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The content must be relevant to the given topics.\\n- Occasional consultation of notes is permitted, but reading from a prepared script loses points.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Content & Relevance\\n- Enunciation\\n- Expression & Engagement\\n- Confidence\\n- Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Cultural Mash up Canvas","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Cultural Mash up Canvas","Sections":{"About":["Canvas painting, solo, on the theme Celebrating 70 Years of India-Oman Relations."],"TimeAndFormat":["The competition lasts 2 hours."],"Rules":["Each participant gets a white canvas (70 cm x 50 cm). Using the canvas given by the organisers is compulsory.","Participants bring their own materials: colours, brushes, palette, water jar, pencils for sketching, rags and similar.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Only acrylic or poster colours may be used. Oil paints, spray paints, digital prints and pre-drawn sketches are not permitted.","Varnish, in spray or liquid form, is strictly prohibited in campus painting.","Stencils and tracing are strictly prohibited."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Relevance to Theme","Creativity & Originality","Composition & Colour Harmony","Execution & Neatness","Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Canvas painting, solo, on the theme Celebrating 70 Years of India-Oman Relations.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The competition lasts 2 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each participant gets a white canvas (70 cm x 50 cm). Using the canvas given by the organisers is compulsory.\\n- Participants bring their own materials: colours, brushes, palette, water jar, pencils for sketching, rags and similar.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Only acrylic or poster colours may be used. Oil paints, spray paints, digital prints and pre-drawn sketches are not permitted.\\n- Varnish, in spray or liquid form, is strictly prohibited in campus painting.\\n- Stencils and tracing are strictly prohibited.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Relevance to Theme\\n- Creativity & Originality\\n- Composition & Colour Harmony\\n- Execution & Neatness\\n- Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Lasya Manjari","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Lasya Manjari","Sections":{"About":["Indian classical dance, solo, titled A Bouquet of Grace."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Styles allowed: Bharatanatyam, Kathak, Mohiniyattam, Odissi or Kuchipudi, in traditional style only.","The theme, music, costumes and make-up must follow the traditional style chosen.","The registration form names the style of dance for each participant.","The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Props are not entertained, except for Kuchipudi."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Make-up, Costume & Accessories","Music","Natya","Nritta","Nritya"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Indian classical dance, solo, titled A Bouquet of Grace.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Styles allowed: Bharatanatyam, Kathak, Mohiniyattam, Odissi or Kuchipudi, in traditional style only.\\n- The theme, music, costumes and make-up must follow the traditional style chosen.\\n- The registration form names the style of dance for each participant.\\n- The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Props are not entertained, except for Kuchipudi.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Make-up, Costume & Accessories\\n- Music\\n- Natya\\n- Nritta\\n- Nritya\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Harmony Haven","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Harmony Haven","Sections":{"About":["Western vocal singing, solo."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one accompaniment is allowed. Contestants bring their own instrument.","Lyrics must be in English only and suitable for school competitions.","Only the song rendition is judged. Background music is not a judging criterion, but it must not hurt the judgement.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Pre-programmed accompaniment on an electronic keyboard, materials, music, MIDI files, MP3 files and karaoke are not allowed."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Choice of Song","Pitch & Dynamics","Voice Texture & Clarity","Pace/ Rhythm","Presentation & Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Western vocal singing, solo.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one accompaniment is allowed. Contestants bring their own instrument.\\n- Lyrics must be in English only and suitable for school competitions.\\n- Only the song rendition is judged. Background music is not a judging criterion, but it must not hurt the judgement.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Pre-programmed accompaniment on an electronic keyboard, materials, music, MIDI files, MP3 files and karaoke are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Choice of Song\\n- Pitch & Dynamics\\n- Voice Texture & Clarity\\n- Pace/ Rhythm\\n- Presentation & Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Elevator Pitch","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Elevator Pitch","Sections":{"About":["Sell Smart, solo, in English. The organisers display a range of products. Each participant picks one product at random and gives a persuasive talk on its features, benefits and why it should be bought."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each participant gets 3 minutes.","Each participant gets 1 minute to look at the chosen product before presenting."],"Rules":["Props or writing materials may be used if needed.","The content must be school-appropriate.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No pre-written notes are allowed during the pitch."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Clarity & Communication Skills","Persuasiveness & Creativity","Confidence & Stage Presence","Use of Language","Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Sell Smart, solo, in English. The organisers display a range of products. Each participant picks one product at random and gives a persuasive talk on its features, benefits and why it should be bought.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each participant gets 3 minutes.\\n- Each participant gets 1 minute to look at the chosen product before presenting.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Props or writing materials may be used if needed.\\n- The content must be school-appropriate.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No pre-written notes are allowed during the pitch.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Clarity & Communication Skills\\n- Persuasiveness & Creativity\\n- Confidence & Stage Presence\\n- Use of Language\\n- Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Punchline Party","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Punchline Party","Sections":{"About":["Stand-up comedy, solo, in English. The theme is open."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each participant gets 4 minutes."],"Rules":["Another language can be used for regionalism only.","The comedy must be original and personal.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No vulgarity, pun, anti-religion or anti-nationalism content. A participant who does this is expelled from the competition immediately.","No background music is allowed."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Clarity","Comedy in Speech","Confidence and Attitude of the Speaker","Stage Presence","Content and Relevance to the Topic"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Stand-up comedy, solo, in English. The theme is open.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each participant gets 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Another language can be used for regionalism only.\\n- The comedy must be original and personal.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No vulgarity, pun, anti-religion or anti-nationalism content. A participant who does this is expelled from the competition immediately.\\n- No background music is allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Clarity\\n- Comedy in Speech\\n- Confidence and Attitude of the Speaker\\n- Stage Presence\\n- Content and Relevance to the Topic\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Raftar Samachar","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Raftar Samachar","Sections":{"About":["On the spot news reading in Hindi, solo. News scrolls on the screen and the participant reads it aloud live like a news anchor. Judging looks at clarity, pronunciation, voice modulation, expression and pace."],"TimeAndFormat":["Each participant gets 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Formal attire is recommended. No additional props are required.","Multiple attempts are not allowed.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Pronunciation & Fluency","Expression & Modulation","Presentation & Posture","Timing & Coordination","Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- On the spot news reading in Hindi, solo. News scrolls on the screen and the participant reads it aloud live like a news anchor. Judging looks at clarity, pronunciation, voice modulation, expression and pace.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Each participant gets 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Formal attire is recommended. No additional props are required.\\n- Multiple attempts are not allowed.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Pronunciation & Fluency\\n- Expression & Modulation\\n- Presentation & Posture\\n- Timing & Coordination\\n- Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Mayoora Vaibhav","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Mayoora Vaibhav","Sections":{"About":["Indian classical dance, solo."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Styles allowed: Bharatanatyam, Kathak, Mohiniyattam, Odissi or Kuchipudi, in traditional style only.","The theme, music, costumes and make-up must follow the traditional style chosen.","The registration form names the style of dance for each participant.","The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Props are not entertained, except for Kuchipudi."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Make-up, Costume & Accessories","Music","Natya","Nritta","Nritya"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Indian classical dance, solo.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Styles allowed: Bharatanatyam, Kathak, Mohiniyattam, Odissi or Kuchipudi, in traditional style only.\\n- The theme, music, costumes and make-up must follow the traditional style chosen.\\n- The registration form names the style of dance for each participant.\\n- The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Props are not entertained, except for Kuchipudi.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Make-up, Costume & Accessories\\n- Music\\n- Natya\\n- Nritta\\n- Nritya\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Poise & Pulse","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Poise & Pulse","Sections":{"About":["Flip dance, solo. Three different kinds of music are played, 1 minute each, and the participant dances instantly to each."],"TimeAndFormat":["The performance lasts 3 minutes in total: 1 minute for each of 3 styles of music."],"Rules":["The participant starts dancing as soon as the music starts and flips when the next music is played. No pause is permitted.","The dance must suit the music played.","Comfortable clothing suitable for dance is allowed. It must be appropriate to school standards and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.","The organisers play the music. The participants get no clue about the music before.","Lots are also taken for the song files.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Musicality - dance synchronisation with Music","Creativity","Technical skill","Energy & Expression","Overall performance quality & impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Flip dance, solo. Three different kinds of music are played, 1 minute each, and the participant dances instantly to each.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The performance lasts 3 minutes in total: 1 minute for each of 3 styles of music.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The participant starts dancing as soon as the music starts and flips when the next music is played. No pause is permitted.\\n- The dance must suit the music played.\\n- Comfortable clothing suitable for dance is allowed. It must be appropriate to school standards and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.\\n- The organisers play the music. The participants get no clue about the music before.\\n- Lots are also taken for the song files.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Musicality - dance synchronisation with Music\\n- Creativity\\n- Technical skill\\n- Energy & Expression\\n- Overall performance quality & impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Moulded Masterpieces","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Moulded Masterpieces","Sections":{"About":["Clay modelling, solo. The theme is open and participants may choose any subject."],"TimeAndFormat":["The competition lasts 3 hours."],"Rules":["The sculpture is at least 1 foot high. Depth and width can vary with the theme and proportion.","The work must be the participant's own creation. No pre-made work or outside help is permitted.","Participants bring their own clay and tools.","The participant gives a 2-line written description of the sculpture at the time of the event.","The sculpture must suit school standards and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No other material is allowed: no thermocol, spray paints, decorative items or pre-moulded parts. Only clay."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Expression of Idea/Theme","Texture & Detailing","Creativity & Originality","Proportion & Balance","Final Finish and Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Clay modelling, solo. The theme is open and participants may choose any subject.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The competition lasts 3 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The sculpture is at least 1 foot high. Depth and width can vary with the theme and proportion.\\n- The work must be the participant's own creation. No pre-made work or outside help is permitted.\\n- Participants bring their own clay and tools.\\n- The participant gives a 2-line written description of the sculpture at the time of the event.\\n- The sculpture must suit school standards and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No other material is allowed: no thermocol, spray paints, decorative items or pre-moulded parts. Only clay.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Expression of Idea/Theme\\n- Texture & Detailing\\n- Creativity & Originality\\n- Proportion & Balance\\n- Final Finish and Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Mystic Mandalas","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Mystic Mandalas","Sections":{"About":["Mandala art, solo. Theme: Harmony in Circles: Balance of Nature & Life. Participants show the balance between nature, humanity and inner peace through mandala patterns."],"TimeAndFormat":["The competition lasts 2 hours."],"Rules":["The artwork must fit within A3 paper (11.7 x 16.5 inches). The host school provides the paper.","Colours, sketch pens, pencils, watercolours or any safe, school-appropriate material can be used.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Only drawing and painting tools are allowed. No pre-made templates or stencils."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Creativity & Originality","Symmetry & Precision","Colour Combination & Aesthetics","Neatness & Technique","Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Mandala art, solo. Theme: Harmony in Circles: Balance of Nature & Life. Participants show the balance between nature, humanity and inner peace through mandala patterns.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The competition lasts 2 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The artwork must fit within A3 paper (11.7 x 16.5 inches). The host school provides the paper.\\n- Colours, sketch pens, pencils, watercolours or any safe, school-appropriate material can be used.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Only drawing and painting tools are allowed. No pre-made templates or stencils.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Creativity & Originality\\n- Symmetry & Precision\\n- Colour Combination & Aesthetics\\n- Neatness & Technique\\n- Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Vocal Vista","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Vocal Vista","Sections":{"About":["Western vocal, solo."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Only one accompaniment is allowed. Contestants bring their own instrument.","Lyrics must be in English only and suitable for school competitions.","Only the song rendition is judged. Background music is not a judging criterion, but it must not hurt the judgement.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Pre-programmed accompaniment on an electronic keyboard, materials, music, MIDI files, MP3 files and karaoke are not allowed."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Choice of Song","Pitch & Dynamics","Voice Texture & Clarity","Pace/ Rhythm","Presentation"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Western vocal, solo.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only one accompaniment is allowed. Contestants bring their own instrument.\\n- Lyrics must be in English only and suitable for school competitions.\\n- Only the song rendition is judged. Background music is not a judging criterion, but it must not hurt the judgement.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Pre-programmed accompaniment on an electronic keyboard, materials, music, MIDI files, MP3 files and karaoke are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Choice of Song\\n- Pitch & Dynamics\\n- Voice Texture & Clarity\\n- Pace/ Rhythm\\n- Presentation\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Soulful Strings","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Soulful Strings","Sections":{"About":["Indian light vocal, solo, in any one Indian language."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Besides a Shruti box or Tanpura (electronic or manual), at most two accompanying instruments (optional) are allowed. Contestants bring their own instruments.","Lyrics must be in one Indian language only and suitable for school competitions.","Only the song rendition is judged. Background music is not a judging criterion, but it must not hurt the judgement.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Film songs are not allowed.","Pre-programmed accompaniments (electronic keyboard and similar), materials, music, MIDI files, MP3 files and karaoke are not allowed."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Choice of Song","Pitch and Dynamics","Voice Texture and Clarity","Melody/ Rhythm","Presentation"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Indian light vocal, solo, in any one Indian language.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Besides a Shruti box or Tanpura (electronic or manual), at most two accompanying instruments (optional) are allowed. Contestants bring their own instruments.\\n- Lyrics must be in one Indian language only and suitable for school competitions.\\n- Only the song rendition is judged. Background music is not a judging criterion, but it must not hurt the judgement.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs are not allowed.\\n- Pre-programmed accompaniments (electronic keyboard and similar), materials, music, MIDI files, MP3 files and karaoke are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Choice of Song\\n- Pitch and Dynamics\\n- Voice Texture and Clarity\\n- Melody/ Rhythm\\n- Presentation\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Cadence Cascade","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Cadence Cascade","Sections":{"About":["Instrumental music on the western keyboard, solo."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Participants use the built-in accompaniments and features of the keyboard only, and bring their own keyboards.","The participant may refer to a music score during the performance if needed.","Contestants are advised not to play piano pieces on the keyboard, because these are not considered for evaluation.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Pre-programmed material such as USB drives, floppy drives, music, MIDI files, MP3 files and karaoke is not allowed."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Choice of Piece","Expression and Dynamics","Technique","Presentation","Use of the keyboard's features"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 participants per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Instrumental music on the western keyboard, solo.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Participants use the built-in accompaniments and features of the keyboard only, and bring their own keyboards.\\n- The participant may refer to a music score during the performance if needed.\\n- Contestants are advised not to play piano pieces on the keyboard, because these are not considered for evaluation.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Pre-programmed material such as USB drives, floppy drives, music, MIDI files, MP3 files and karaoke is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Choice of Piece\\n- Expression and Dynamics\\n- Technique\\n- Presentation\\n- Use of the keyboard's features\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 participants per school."},{"Title":"Grace Mosaic","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Grace Mosaic","Sections":{"About":["Contemporary dance, group. Contemporary dance does not permit the classical technique in favour of modern dances. It is not necessarily a narrative art form, choreography relies on technique, and it permits multiple simultaneous actions and unpredictable changes in rhythm, speed and direction."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students.","The theme, choreography, costumes and make-up must suit school competitions and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.","The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Film songs are not permitted."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Rhythm & Synchronisation","Elements of Dance","Costumes & Accessories","Entry, Exit Formation & Choreography","Presentation & Audience Appeal"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Contemporary dance, group. Contemporary dance does not permit the classical technique in favour of modern dances. It is not necessarily a narrative art form, choreography relies on technique, and it permits multiple simultaneous actions and unpredictable changes in rhythm, speed and direction.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students.\\n- The theme, choreography, costumes and make-up must suit school competitions and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.\\n- The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs are not permitted.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Rhythm & Synchronisation\\n- Elements of Dance\\n- Costumes & Accessories\\n- Entry, Exit Formation & Choreography\\n- Presentation & Audience Appeal\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."},{"Title":"Roots Rejoice","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Roots Rejoice","Sections":{"About":["Indian folk dance, group."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 6 minutes."],"Rules":["Each school can send two teams of at least 6 and at most 8 students.","The theme, costumes and make-up must suit school competitions and respect the culture and traditions of India and Oman.","The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Elements of Dance","Rhythm & Synchronization","Make up, Costume & Accessories","Entry, Exit Formation & Choreography","Presentation & Audience Appeal"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 teams of 6 to 8 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Indian folk dance, group.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 6 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school can send two teams of at least 6 and at most 8 students.\\n- The theme, costumes and make-up must suit school competitions and respect the culture and traditions of India and Oman.\\n- The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Elements of Dance\\n- Rhythm & Synchronization\\n- Make up, Costume & Accessories\\n- Entry, Exit Formation & Choreography\\n- Presentation & Audience Appeal\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 teams of 6 to 8 students per school."},{"Title":"Natya Vihar","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Natya Vihar","Sections":{"About":["Indian classical dance, group."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students.","The style must be one of: Bharatanatyam, Kuchipudi, Mohiniyattam, Kathak or Odissi.","The theme, costumes and make-up must suit the dance style and school competitions in Oman.","The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Props are not entertained."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Rhythm & Synchronisation","Natya, Nritta, Nritya","Costumes & Accessories","Entry, Exit Formation & Choreography","Presentation & Audience Appeal"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Indian classical dance, group.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students.\\n- The style must be one of: Bharatanatyam, Kuchipudi, Mohiniyattam, Kathak or Odissi.\\n- The theme, costumes and make-up must suit the dance style and school competitions in Oman.\\n- The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Props are not entertained.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Rhythm & Synchronisation\\n- Natya, Nritta, Nritya\\n- Costumes & Accessories\\n- Entry, Exit Formation & Choreography\\n- Presentation & Audience Appeal\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."},{"Title":"Vibe Voltage","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Vibe Voltage","Sections":{"About":["Western rock band, group, live music only."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes.","Each band gets a set-up time of 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students, singers and instrumentalists included.","The host school provides a standard drum set. Every band brings its own other instruments.","Songs must be of the Rock genre, in English only, with decent, acceptable lyrics.","Each band performs live music only.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Stage Presence","Coordination","Creativity & Improvisation","Harmony","Audience Engagement"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Western rock band, group, live music only.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n- Each band gets a set-up time of 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students, singers and instrumentalists included.\\n- The host school provides a standard drum set. Every band brings its own other instruments.\\n- Songs must be of the Rock genre, in English only, with decent, acceptable lyrics.\\n- Each band performs live music only.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Stage Presence\\n- Coordination\\n- Creativity & Improvisation\\n- Harmony\\n- Audience Engagement\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."},{"Title":"Street Percussion","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Street Percussion","Sections":{"About":["Junk jams, group, live music only. The style is rhythmic, energetic and engaging, fused with claps and stomps."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students.","Participants bring their own non-traditional everyday items such as buckets, tins, bottles and sticks.","Costume: casual or street style. Uniformity within the group is preferred.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No conventional musical instruments are permitted.","No vocals are permitted."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Rhythm & synchronization","Creativity of materials used","Stage presence & coordination","Vibe and Energy","Overall impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Junk jams, group, live music only. The style is rhythmic, energetic and engaging, fused with claps and stomps.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students.\\n- Participants bring their own non-traditional everyday items such as buckets, tins, bottles and sticks.\\n- Costume: casual or street style. Uniformity within the group is preferred.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No conventional musical instruments are permitted.\\n- No vocals are permitted.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Rhythm & synchronization\\n- Creativity of materials used\\n- Stage presence & coordination\\n- Vibe and Energy\\n- Overall impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."},{"Title":"Desi Dhun","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Desi Dhun","Sections":{"About":["Indian folk song, group. Only traditional Indian folk songs are permitted."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Each school sends one team of at least 8 and at most 10 students, singers and instrumentalists included.","The folk song may be in any recognised Indian language or dialect, but it must be a genuine folk rendition.","Participants are encouraged to wear attire that reflects the culture of the folk tradition.","Only live accompaniment is allowed. At most three participants may play instruments, each only one instrument of any type. They count within the maximum team size of 10. Contestants bring their own instruments.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Film songs are strictly prohibited.","Pre-programmed music is not allowed."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Choice of Song","Coordination","Creativity & Improvisation","Harmony","Presentation"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 1 team of 8 to 10 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Indian folk song, group. Only traditional Indian folk songs are permitted.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends one team of at least 8 and at most 10 students, singers and instrumentalists included.\\n- The folk song may be in any recognised Indian language or dialect, but it must be a genuine folk rendition.\\n- Participants are encouraged to wear attire that reflects the culture of the folk tradition.\\n- Only live accompaniment is allowed. At most three participants may play instruments, each only one instrument of any type. They count within the maximum team size of 10. Contestants bring their own instruments.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs are strictly prohibited.\\n- Pre-programmed music is not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Choice of Song\\n- Coordination\\n- Creativity & Improvisation\\n- Harmony\\n- Presentation\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 1 team of 8 to 10 students per school."},{"Title":"Unplugged Unity","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Unplugged Unity","Sections":{"About":["A cappella, group. Theme: Indian patriotic songs. The presentation must be strictly vocal."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 4 minutes."],"Rules":["Each school sends two teams of at least 8 and at most 10 students.","Teams may use body percussion, humming, beatboxing or vocal effects.","The performance must suit school standards.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Film songs are not permitted.","No instrumental accompaniment or pre-recorded music.","No offensive or inappropriate content."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Pitching, Rhythm & Diction","Harmony and Synchronization","Creativity and Vocal Effects","Expression and Stage Presence","Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 teams of 8 to 10 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- A cappella, group. Theme: Indian patriotic songs. The presentation must be strictly vocal.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 4 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends two teams of at least 8 and at most 10 students.\\n- Teams may use body percussion, humming, beatboxing or vocal effects.\\n- The performance must suit school standards.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Film songs are not permitted.\\n- No instrumental accompaniment or pre-recorded music.\\n- No offensive or inappropriate content.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Pitching, Rhythm & Diction\\n- Harmony and Synchronization\\n- Creativity and Vocal Effects\\n- Expression and Stage Presence\\n- Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 teams of 8 to 10 students per school."},{"Title":"Patchwork Palette","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Patchwork Palette","Sections":{"About":["Collage making, group of 2. Theme: Celebrating 70 Years of India-Oman Relations. Teams can show shared heritage, trade, culture, education and people-to-people ties."],"TimeAndFormat":["The competition lasts 3 hours."],"Rules":["Each school sends two teams of 2 students.","Every team gets a drawing sheet (70 cm x 50 cm). Using the drawing paper given by the organisers is compulsory.","Participants bring their own art materials.","Allowed materials: any type of paper (newspaper, colour, crepe, waste), dry leaves, flower petals, grass, pencil scraping curls, gilt, cloth and waste material. Scissors, blades and cutters may be used for cutting.","Printed photographs and pictures and pre-drawn articles can be used as a unit but not as a whole picture.","A pencil can be used only for outline drawing. A border, if any, must be made with allowed materials only.","Appropriate slogans, quotations and captions can be used.","The participant chest number must be attached to the collage.","Participants may refer to pictures and photographs while making the collage, and may trace a prepared outline of the design onto the given sheet in the allotted time.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No colours of any kind (water, crayon, oil, spray and similar)."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Presentation of Theme","Composition","Colour Scheme","Material Selection","Creativity & Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 teams of 2 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Collage making, group of 2. Theme: Celebrating 70 Years of India-Oman Relations. Teams can show shared heritage, trade, culture, education and people-to-people ties.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The competition lasts 3 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends two teams of 2 students.\\n- Every team gets a drawing sheet (70 cm x 50 cm). Using the drawing paper given by the organisers is compulsory.\\n- Participants bring their own art materials.\\n- Allowed materials: any type of paper (newspaper, colour, crepe, waste), dry leaves, flower petals, grass, pencil scraping curls, gilt, cloth and waste material. Scissors, blades and cutters may be used for cutting.\\n- Printed photographs and pictures and pre-drawn articles can be used as a unit but not as a whole picture.\\n- A pencil can be used only for outline drawing. A border, if any, must be made with allowed materials only.\\n- Appropriate slogans, quotations and captions can be used.\\n- The participant chest number must be attached to the collage.\\n- Participants may refer to pictures and photographs while making the collage, and may trace a prepared outline of the design onto the given sheet in the allotted time.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No colours of any kind (water, crayon, oil, spray and similar).\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Presentation of Theme\\n- Composition\\n- Colour Scheme\\n- Material Selection\\n- Creativity & Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 teams of 2 students per school."},{"Title":"Frozen Frames","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Frozen Frames","Sections":{"About":["Tableau, group. Theme: National Integration (India). Style: static presentation."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 3 minutes."],"Rules":["Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students.","Narration, if used, must be pre-recorded.","Teams may use costumes and properties that suit the theme and school standards.","The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Live music and live speaking are not allowed."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Costume, Props & Makeup","Theme relevance & originality","Expression & presentation","Synchronization & stage coverage","Overall impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Tableau, group. Theme: National Integration (India). Style: static presentation.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students.\\n- Narration, if used, must be pre-recorded.\\n- Teams may use costumes and properties that suit the theme and school standards.\\n- The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Live music and live speaking are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Costume, Props & Makeup\\n- Theme relevance & originality\\n- Expression & presentation\\n- Synchronization & stage coverage\\n- Overall impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."},{"Title":"Enchanted Shapes","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Enchanted Shapes","Sections":{"About":["Illusion sculpture, group. Theme: Birds, one or more, sitting, perching or in natural poses. The team creates a 3D visual artwork or optical illusion that gives a depth or perspective trick."],"TimeAndFormat":["The event lasts 3 hours. The final display must be static."],"Rules":["Each school sends one team of at most 4 students.","The medium is an open choice (cardboard, thermocol, clay, recyclable materials, parts of metal and similar), but it must be safe and school-appropriate.","The artwork must not be bigger than 1 ft x 1 ft x 1 ft.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Hanging displays are not allowed.","Pre-made or ready-made sculptures are not accepted."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Creativity & originality","Technique & finishing","Illusion effect/ visual effect/ 3D","Theme interpretation","Overall aesthetic appeal"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 1 team of up to 4 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Illusion sculpture, group. Theme: Birds, one or more, sitting, perching or in natural poses. The team creates a 3D visual artwork or optical illusion that gives a depth or perspective trick.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The event lasts 3 hours. The final display must be static.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends one team of at most 4 students.\\n- The medium is an open choice (cardboard, thermocol, clay, recyclable materials, parts of metal and similar), but it must be safe and school-appropriate.\\n- The artwork must not be bigger than 1 ft x 1 ft x 1 ft.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Hanging displays are not allowed.\\n- Pre-made or ready-made sculptures are not accepted.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Creativity & originality\\n- Technique & finishing\\n- Illusion effect/ visual effect/ 3D\\n- Theme interpretation\\n- Overall aesthetic appeal\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 1 team of up to 4 students per school."},{"Title":"Wordless Wonders","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Wordless Wonders","Sections":{"About":["Mime, group. The theme is open, but only positive social themes can be presented."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 7 minutes, including the introduction."],"Rules":["Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students.","The team must introduce the mime by stating its title and theme, in only a very short theme narration of 2 to 3 sentences.","Only gestures and movements are allowed during the mime, with appropriate mime make-up. Mime face make-up and costumes are allowed. Sign boards and placards may be used.","Background music (live or recorded) is compulsory. The musical accompaniment must have no lyrics or human vocal sounds. A common music and sound system is provided.","The theme, costumes and make-up must suit school competitions and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.","The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No religious, political or controversial themes.","No dialogues or words, no lip synching and no audible sounds by the performers.","Props and theatrical, drama, dance or character make-up are not allowed."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Execution of theme","Direction","Action/miming","Synchronisation & Coordination","Music, Make-up & Costume"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Mime, group. The theme is open, but only positive social themes can be presented.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 7 minutes, including the introduction.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends one team of at least 6 and at most 8 students.\\n- The team must introduce the mime by stating its title and theme, in only a very short theme narration of 2 to 3 sentences.\\n- Only gestures and movements are allowed during the mime, with appropriate mime make-up. Mime face make-up and costumes are allowed. Sign boards and placards may be used.\\n- Background music (live or recorded) is compulsory. The musical accompaniment must have no lyrics or human vocal sounds. A common music and sound system is provided.\\n- The theme, costumes and make-up must suit school competitions and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.\\n- The audio USB (Windows Media Player compatible, audio track only) goes to the Event Coordinator 30 minutes before the event. Keep a backup USB.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No religious, political or controversial themes.\\n- No dialogues or words, no lip synching and no audible sounds by the performers.\\n- Props and theatrical, drama, dance or character make-up are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Execution of theme\\n- Direction\\n- Action/miming\\n- Synchronisation & Coordination\\n- Music, Make-up & Costume\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 1 team of 6 to 8 students per school."},{"Title":"Unbound Voices","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Unbound Voices","Sections":{"About":["Street play in English, group. The theme is open, but only positive social themes can be presented."],"TimeAndFormat":["Maximum 8 minutes, including the introduction."],"Rules":["Each school sends one team of at least 8 and at most 10 students.","The play is in English. Certain expressions may be in an Indian language, but English must stay the main language.","The team must introduce the play by stating its title and theme.","The theme, costumes, props, dialogues and make-up must suit school competitions and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.","Props and music (live only) are permitted.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No religious, political or controversial themes.","No prompting and no script.","Light adjustments are not allowed."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Costumes, Props & Use of Space","Execution of Theme & Climax","Acting","Direction","Overall Impact & Audience Appeal"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 1 team of 8 to 10 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Street play in English, group. The theme is open, but only positive social themes can be presented.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Maximum 8 minutes, including the introduction.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends one team of at least 8 and at most 10 students.\\n- The play is in English. Certain expressions may be in an Indian language, but English must stay the main language.\\n- The team must introduce the play by stating its title and theme.\\n- The theme, costumes, props, dialogues and make-up must suit school competitions and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.\\n- Props and music (live only) are permitted.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No religious, political or controversial themes.\\n- No prompting and no script.\\n- Light adjustments are not allowed.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Costumes, Props & Use of Space\\n- Execution of Theme & Climax\\n- Acting\\n- Direction\\n- Overall Impact & Audience Appeal\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 1 team of 8 to 10 students per school."},{"Title":"Promo Pulse","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Promo Pulse","Sections":{"About":["Digital ad-making video, group. Target: an advertisement that promotes Digital Wellness: Using technology responsibly."],"TimeAndFormat":["The advertisement is 30 to 45 seconds long."],"Rules":["Each school sends two teams of at most 4 students.","The work must be original, not an advertisement already used in the industry. Avoid ready-made videos from video-making apps or templates.","A video camera, animation software and similar tools can be used. The organisers do not provide cameras, software, computers or other gadgets.","No unethical scenes. Footers such as Statutory Warning or Creative Animation, if needed, are given as in any standard advertisement.","The theme, dialogues, animations, costumes and make-up must suit school competitions and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.","Each team submits two versions in the Google Drive shared with the School Coordinator. File 1, for judging, holds only the advertisement, with no school or participant names (a team that reveals the school is disqualified). File 2, for screening, also holds the cast, crew, full names and school name as end credits.","Entries are sent by the Google Drive link to the host school email by {{AdSubmissionDeadline}}.","Participants need not be at the venue while the advertisement is judged. The teacher coordinator may be present if they wish.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Advertisements sent for any earlier contest are disqualified."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Concept","Editing","Creativity","Presentation (quality of video, animation, lighting)","Customer Persuasion"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 teams of up to 4 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Digital ad-making video, group. Target: an advertisement that promotes Digital Wellness: Using technology responsibly.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The advertisement is 30 to 45 seconds long.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends two teams of at most 4 students.\\n- The work must be original, not an advertisement already used in the industry. Avoid ready-made videos from video-making apps or templates.\\n- A video camera, animation software and similar tools can be used. The organisers do not provide cameras, software, computers or other gadgets.\\n- No unethical scenes. Footers such as Statutory Warning or Creative Animation, if needed, are given as in any standard advertisement.\\n- The theme, dialogues, animations, costumes and make-up must suit school competitions and respect the culture and traditions of Oman.\\n- Each team submits two versions in the Google Drive shared with the School Coordinator. File 1, for judging, holds only the advertisement, with no school or participant names (a team that reveals the school is disqualified). File 2, for screening, also holds the cast, crew, full names and school name as end credits.\\n- Entries are sent by the Google Drive link to the host school email by {{AdSubmissionDeadline}}.\\n- Participants need not be at the venue while the advertisement is judged. The teacher coordinator may be present if they wish.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Advertisements sent for any earlier contest are disqualified.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Concept\\n- Editing\\n- Creativity\\n- Presentation (quality of video, animation, lighting)\\n- Customer Persuasion\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 teams of up to 4 students per school."},{"Title":"Lens Legacy","Source":"ISTF 2025 Handbook Rules & Regulations for the Competitive Events: Lens Legacy","Sections":{"About":["Digital photography and album making, group. Theme: Cultural Kaleidoscope. Culture must be shown respectfully and positively, without hurting the sentiments of any community."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Each school sends two teams of at most 4 students.","Camera: 10 megapixel minimum.","The album holds 25 to 30 photographs. Each photo is at least 5 x 7 inches (larger is allowed).","Photo editing and album-making software is allowed.","Only the hardcopy album is submitted to the Event Coordinator at the venue 30 minutes before the competition. The school can collect it after the results are displayed. The host school is not responsible for albums not collected.","The school Principal certifies that the album was made only by school students, without the help of adults.","The organisers do not provide cameras, software, computers or other gadgets.","Participants need not be at the venue while the album is judged. The teacher coordinator may be present if they wish.","Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["Photos downloaded from the internet. If found, the entry is disqualified."],"Judging":["Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.","Required Elements of Photography","Focus (sharpness of subject), Lighting & Composition","Theme (execution of the theme in a creative way)","Album design: Creativity & Print Quality","Overall Impact"],"Points":null,"Notes":["Entry limit: 2 teams of up to 4 students per school."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Digital photography and album making, group. Theme: Cultural Kaleidoscope. Culture must be shown respectfully and positively, without hurting the sentiments of any community.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Each school sends two teams of at most 4 students.\\n- Camera: 10 megapixel minimum.\\n- The album holds 25 to 30 photographs. Each photo is at least 5 x 7 inches (larger is allowed).\\n- Photo editing and album-making software is allowed.\\n- Only the hardcopy album is submitted to the Event Coordinator at the venue 30 minutes before the competition. The school can collect it after the results are displayed. The host school is not responsible for albums not collected.\\n- The school Principal certifies that the album was made only by school students, without the help of adults.\\n- The organisers do not provide cameras, software, computers or other gadgets.\\n- Participants need not be at the venue while the album is judged. The teacher coordinator may be present if they wish.\\n- Also see the general rules for reporting time, time limit, performance order, chest number, calls for the stage, points, trophies and certificates.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- Photos downloaded from the internet. If found, the entry is disqualified.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Judged out of 50 marks. Each criterion is worth 10 points.\\n- Required Elements of Photography\\n- Focus (sharpness of subject), Lighting & Composition\\n- Theme (execution of the theme in a creative way)\\n- Album design: Creativity & Print Quality\\n- Overall Impact\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Entry limit: 2 teams of up to 4 students per school."}]`),s=[],r=[{Key:"EventDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Festival dates (2025 edition)",Value:"13 and 14 November 2025 (Thursday and Friday)",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook cover and p.6"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Festival venue (2025 edition)",Value:{Name:"Indian School Al Maabela",Address:"Postal Code: 122, Al Maabela",City:"Sultanate of Oman",MapUrl:"",Directions:"Reporting: ISTF Office, Room no. 3, Ground Floor, B Wing. Participants enter by Gate No. 4 on the opening day."},Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.38 contact details and p.6 rule 12"},{Key:"RegistrationDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date for registration (2025 edition)",Value:"2025-10-23",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.6 rule 9"},{Key:"NameChangeDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to change participant names (2025 edition)",Value:"2025-10-28",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.6 rule 10"},{Key:"CancellationNoticeDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date by which schools are told of cancelled events (2025 edition)",Value:"2025-10-23",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.6 rule 13"},{Key:"AdSubmissionDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date for the digital ad video (2025 edition)",Value:"2025-11-10",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.35 Promo Pulse rule k"},{Key:"CwsnVideoDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date for Wonder Weavers' Talent videos (2025 edition)",Value:"2025-10-30",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.37 Wonder Weavers' Talent rule b"},{Key:"ReconfirmationTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Reconfirmation of entry lists (2025 edition)",Value:"Thursday 13 November 2025, 7.00 a.m. to 8.00 a.m., ISTF Office (Room no. 3, Ground Floor, B Wing)",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.6 rule 12"},{Key:"InauguralTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Inaugural function (2025 edition)",Value:"13 November 2025 at 7:30 a.m. in the school Multi-Purpose Hall; Student Team Leaders report at Gate No. 4 at 7:00 a.m.; everyone seated by 8:35 a.m.",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.9"},{Key:"ValedictoryTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Valedictory function (2025 edition)",Value:"14 November 2025 at 6:00 p.m. in the school Multi-Purpose Hall; everyone seated by 5:30 p.m.",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.9"},{Key:"SessionReportingTimes",Kind:"time",Label:"Reporting time at event venues (2025 edition)",Value:"30 minutes before the scheduled start of the event; morning session 7:30 a.m., afternoon session 1:30 p.m.",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.11 rule 7"},{Key:"UsbSubmissionTime",Kind:"time",Label:"Time to hand in audio USB, album and lots",Value:"30 minutes before the scheduled start of the event",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.10 rule 4 and p.11 rule 6"},{Key:"UtarUsbDeadline",Kind:"time",Label:"UTAR USB submission (2025 edition)",Value:"At the ISTF Office on the first day before 10:30 a.m.",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.37 UTAR rule f"},{Key:"GrievanceFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Fee for each grievance",Value:"RO 100 (Rial Omani one hundred) for every grievance, refunded if the grievance is upheld",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.11 rule 8 iii and iv"},{Key:"EntryFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry fee",Value:"No entry fee is printed in the handbook",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook General Information"},{Key:"PhotoSpec",Kind:"text",Label:"Participant photograph specification",Value:"Minimum 1800 x 1200 pixels, JPEG only, file size 1 MB to 3 MB, in school uniform",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.12 rule 9"},{Key:"SoloPhotoFileName",Kind:"text",Label:"File name for a solo participant photograph",Value:"School's Abbreviation_Event Name_Name of the participant (example: ISAM_Printopia_Helen)",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.12 rule 9 note"},{Key:"TeamPhotoFileName",Kind:"text",Label:"File name for a team photograph",Value:"School's Abbreviation_Event Name (example: ISAM_Team1_Roots Rejoice or ISAM_Team2_Roots Rejoice)",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.12 rule 9 note"},{Key:"RegistrationEmail",Kind:"text",Label:"Email for entry forms, name changes and feedback (2025 edition)",Value:"istf2025@indianschoolmaabela.com",Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.6 rules 9, 10 and 20, p.38"},{Key:"LeadCoordinator",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contact: Lead Coordinator (2025 edition)",Value:{Name:"Ms. Srividya Ramkumar",Role:"Lead Coordinator, AVP Co-scholastic, Indian School Al Maabela",Phone:"92136834",WhatsApp:"",Email:"istf2025@indianschoolmaabela.com"},Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.38"},{Key:"AccommodationContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contact: accommodation (2025 edition)",Value:{Name:"Mr. Vimosh V.",Role:"Accommodation enquiries",Phone:"00968-90562072",WhatsApp:"",Email:""},Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.7 rule 17 d"},{Key:"SchoolOffice",Kind:"contact",Label:"Contact: Principal's Office (2025 edition)",Value:{Name:"Indian School Al Maabela",Role:"Principal's Office",Phone:"+968 24456891",WhatsApp:"",Email:""},Source:"ISTF 2025 Handbook p.38"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"News printed in the source",Value:[{Date:"2026-09-23",Title:"Indian School Talent Fest 2026: 4 and 5 November 2026 at Indian School Boushar",Text:"Under the aegis of the Board of Directors, Indian School Boushar invites participants from all the Indian Schools in Oman to ISTF 2026 on Wednesday 4 and Thursday 5 November 2026 at Indian School Boushar, for classes I to XII. Competitive events are in four categories: Preparatory Stage (classes III, IV, V), Middle Stage (classes VI, VII, VIII), Secondary Stage (classes IX, X, XI, XII) and the Open Category (classes I to XII). UTAR and CWSN are non-competitive events for classes I to XII. The Foundational Stage (classes I and II) has school-level competitive events. The 2026 rules say a student may take part in up to two events: two solo events on the same day (one morning, one afternoon), two group events on the same day, one group and one solo event on the same day, or two solo or two group events on different days. As printed by one member school, entries went by Google Form and a school-level screening was held first; a student chosen for more than two events picks the best two, and a school may allow more than two when there are too few participants. The 2026 handbook was not available when this was written.",Url:""},{Date:"2025-10-19",Title:"Indian School Talent Fest 2025 handbook: 33 competitive events at Indian School Al Maabela",Text:"The handbook, dated 19 October 2025, announces ISTF 2025 on 13 and 14 November 2025 at Indian School Al Maabela, with 33 competitive events (19 solo events and 14 group events) and two non-competitive items, UTAR and Wonder Weavers' Talent.",Url:"https://ismoman.com/PDFDOCUMENTS/ISTF%202025%20@ISAM%20HANDBOOK%20%2019.10.25.pdf"}],Source:"Indian School Nizwa circular on ISTF 2026 (23 September 2026); ISTF 2025 Handbook cover"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules, dates, contacts, grievance fee and entry limits of ISTF 2025 and the 2026 dates.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"Indian School Talent Fest 2025 Handbook (Indian School Al Maabela); Indian School Nizwa circular 2026-27 on ISTF 2026",Url:"https://ismoman.com/PDFDOCUMENTS/ISTF%202025%20@ISAM%20HANDBOOK%20%2019.10.25.pdf"}],d={TemplateKey:e,Year:2025,Note:t,Page:o,ParticipantTypes:n,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:a,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:r,Evidence:l};export{i as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,a as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,o as Page,n as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,r as Variables,c as Year,d as default};
